1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,000
Hello everyone, this video will introduce you to 3D clothing production, related tools for simulation control.

2
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:17,000
First, in the Connect tab, under the CloudTraining account, unlock the keyword simulation control.

3
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:27,000
First, double-click to download and open the frozen and back-up file.

4
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:32,000
In the 3D window, select the belt of this shirt skirt.

5
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:37,000
Right-click to select Frozen, and Ctrl-K.

6
00:00:37,000 --> 00:00:41,000
The frozen version will appear light blue on the surface.

7
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:48,000
After opening the simulation, its position and shape will be completely fixed, and drag will not change or shift.

8
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:56,000
But it should be noted that there is still physical contact and collision between it and the normal soft clothing below.

9
00:00:57,000 --> 00:01:01,000
Then we right-click on the plate again.

10
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:03,000
Unlock the belt.

11
00:01:03,000 --> 00:01:06,000
Then right-click to switch to the back-up plate.

12
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:11,000
Right-click, Ctrl-J.

13
00:01:11,000 --> 00:01:15,000
The back-up plate becomes translucent blue.

14
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:24,000
After opening the simulation, you can see that the back-up plate is not only fixed, but also no longer involved in any collision calculation.

15
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:27,000
The drag material will be directly worn through.

16
00:01:27,000 --> 00:01:33,000
This also means that in the simulation, the back-up plate is a relatively frozen plate.

17
00:01:33,000 --> 00:01:35,000
The calculation is smaller.

18
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:38,000
After stopping the simulation, return to the state of not wearing a mask.

19
00:01:38,000 --> 00:01:41,000
On the plate, you will see the back-up plate again.

20
00:01:41,000 --> 00:01:48,000
In addition, at the bottom of the back-up plate, there are options for the back-up plate and the sewing line.

21
00:01:48,000 --> 00:01:56,000
If you choose the back-up plate and the sewing line, not only will the plate fail, but the sewing line relationship associated with it will also temporarily break.

22
00:01:56,000 --> 00:02:00,000
And the sewing line will turn white.

23
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:04,000
Take this suit as an example.

24
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:06,000
On one side, the back-up plate.

25
00:02:06,000 --> 00:02:10,000
On the other side, the back-up plate and the sewing line.

26
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:17,000
You will find that the back-up plate retains the sewing line relationship with the sleeve plate on one side.

27
00:02:17,000 --> 00:02:21,000
On the other side, the back-up plate and the sewing line are reversed.

28
00:02:21,000 --> 00:02:24,000
The back-up plate is equivalent to temporarily non-existence.

29
00:02:24,000 --> 00:02:28,000
In addition, the sewing line relationship is also broken.

30
00:02:28,000 --> 00:02:30,000
Stop the simulation.

31
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:32,000
Activate the sewing curve.

32
00:02:32,000 --> 00:02:37,000
Simulate to stabilize.

33
00:02:37,000 --> 00:02:42,000
In the actual application, when adjusting the clothing shape and simulating complex clothing,

34
00:02:42,000 --> 00:02:48,000
you can use the freeze and counter-activation to fix the plate shape and reduce the calculation,

35
00:02:48,000 --> 00:02:51,000
thereby increasing the simulation efficiency.

36
00:02:51,000 --> 00:02:52,000
For example, now,

37
00:02:52,000 --> 00:02:58,000
we need to move the belt from the left side of the shirt skirt to the right side.

38
00:02:58,000 --> 00:03:00,000
If you directly turn on the simulation,

39
00:03:00,000 --> 00:03:02,000
directly drag the belt plate,

40
00:03:02,000 --> 00:03:05,000
you will find that the speed of adjusting the belt is slower,

41
00:03:05,000 --> 00:03:07,000
because when the belt moves,

42
00:03:07,000 --> 00:03:10,000
the whole clothes are involved in the simulation.

43
00:03:10,000 --> 00:03:13,000
In order to speed up the simulation,

44
00:03:13,000 --> 00:03:14,000
reduce the calculation,

45
00:03:14,000 --> 00:03:18,000
we can freeze the plate that has direct contact with the belt.

46
00:03:18,000 --> 00:03:21,000
Because the collision calculation of clothing and belt needs to be maintained,

47
00:03:21,000 --> 00:03:23,000
that is, the collision,

48
00:03:23,000 --> 00:03:29,000
the other plates that are not in contact with each other are all counter-activated.

49
00:03:29,000 --> 00:03:34,000
Then turn on the simulation.

50
00:03:34,000 --> 00:03:37,000
Adjust the belt position.

51
00:03:37,000 --> 00:03:40,000
You will find that the simulation speed will be much faster.

52
00:03:40,000 --> 00:03:50,000
After adjusting the belt position,

53
00:03:50,000 --> 00:03:52,000
on the 3D window,

54
00:03:52,000 --> 00:03:53,000
on the clothing,

55
00:03:53,000 --> 00:03:54,000
any position double click,

56
00:03:54,000 --> 00:03:56,000
select the whole clothing,

57
00:03:56,000 --> 00:04:00,000
right-click to select activation.

58
00:04:00,000 --> 00:04:02,000
Re-model,

59
00:04:02,000 --> 00:04:10,000
the belt is naturally worn.

60
00:04:10,000 --> 00:04:14,000
Here we see the reset arrangement together.

61
00:04:14,000 --> 00:04:17,000
Open the reset arrangement file,

62
00:04:20,000 --> 00:04:22,000
when the clothing appears,

63
00:04:22,000 --> 00:04:24,000
how to fix it.

64
00:04:24,000 --> 00:04:26,000
Take this clothing as an example,

65
00:04:26,000 --> 00:04:28,000
you can see the bottom of the skirt,

66
00:04:28,000 --> 00:04:31,000
the collar and sleeves have problems.

67
00:04:31,000 --> 00:04:33,000
First see the bottom,

68
00:04:33,000 --> 00:04:35,000
here the front and back pieces of the side,

69
00:04:35,000 --> 00:04:38,000
are made in two different ways.

70
00:04:38,000 --> 00:04:41,000
The front piece is added directly by the side tool.

71
00:04:41,000 --> 00:04:43,000
For the wear problem in front of the eye,

72
00:04:43,000 --> 00:04:46,000
we can directly on the side of the wear,

73
00:04:46,000 --> 00:04:48,000
right-click to choose to arrange initialization,

74
00:04:48,000 --> 00:04:51,000
you can quickly put the side

75
00:04:51,000 --> 00:04:53,000
on the inside of the bottom of the front piece,

76
00:04:53,000 --> 00:04:56,000
and then re-model it.

77
00:04:56,000 --> 00:04:58,000
The back piece of the side,

78
00:04:58,000 --> 00:05:02,000
is sewn on by the created side plate.

79
00:05:02,000 --> 00:05:05,000
First, we can also use a similar tool,

80
00:05:05,000 --> 00:05:08,000
put the side to the inside of the bottom of the back piece,

81
00:05:08,000 --> 00:05:10,000
right-click on the side of the back piece,

82
00:05:10,000 --> 00:05:12,000
choose to add to the inside,

83
00:05:12,000 --> 00:05:16,000
you can add the side to the inside.

84
00:05:16,000 --> 00:05:17,000
This is suitable for two plates,

85
00:05:17,000 --> 00:05:20,000
used when there is a seam relationship.

86
00:05:20,000 --> 00:05:23,000
If the outer layer of the fabric is twisted,

87
00:05:23,000 --> 00:05:24,000
the impact is too big,

88
00:05:24,000 --> 00:05:26,000
and the addition to the inside is not possible to solve,

89
00:05:26,000 --> 00:05:29,000
you can select the side of the problem first,

90
00:05:29,000 --> 00:05:33,000
right-click to set the anti-aggression plate and sewing line,

91
00:05:33,000 --> 00:05:36,000
note that because it is necessary to completely eliminate the side of the side,

92
00:05:36,000 --> 00:05:41,000
so it must be the option of the anti-aggression plate and sewing line.

93
00:05:43,000 --> 00:05:44,000
Open the simulation,

94
00:05:44,000 --> 00:05:46,000
so that the sound is natural and smooth,

95
00:05:46,000 --> 00:05:58,000
then re-activate the side and add to the inside.

96
00:05:58,000 --> 00:06:02,000
The problem of overlapping the wrong position of the top and the sleeve,

97
00:06:02,000 --> 00:06:06,000
you can try to solve it by resetting the 3D arrangement position of the plate,

98
00:06:06,000 --> 00:06:10,000
we only need to select two plates at the same time.

99
00:06:10,000 --> 00:06:13,000
Right-click to reset the 3D arrangement position,

100
00:06:13,000 --> 00:06:17,000
because these plates have previously used the arrangement point,

101
00:06:17,000 --> 00:06:20,000
there is a memory in the arrangement file,

102
00:06:20,000 --> 00:06:23,000
the plate can return to the 3D arrangement state,

103
00:06:23,000 --> 00:06:26,000
re-modeling can be restored to normal.

104
00:06:28,000 --> 00:06:30,000
If the button is stuck in,

105
00:06:30,000 --> 00:06:33,000
right-click to reset the button.

106
00:06:35,000 --> 00:06:39,000
The sleeve and the sleeve plate are also the same operation.

107
00:06:39,000 --> 00:06:42,000
Select them together,

108
00:06:42,000 --> 00:06:45,000
right-click to reset the 3D arrangement position.

109
00:06:45,000 --> 00:06:51,000
You can see that the sleeve plate has been reset to the 3D position,

110
00:06:51,000 --> 00:06:54,000
and the sleeve plate has no arrangement memory,

111
00:06:54,000 --> 00:06:56,000
so it is flat.

112
00:06:56,000 --> 00:06:58,000
In this case,

113
00:06:58,000 --> 00:07:01,000
we can reopen the virtual model arrangement point,

114
00:07:01,000 --> 00:07:03,000
select the plate,

115
00:07:03,000 --> 00:07:06,000
re-select the arrangement point to be arranged,

116
00:07:09,000 --> 00:07:14,000
or this side-mounted plate,

117
00:07:14,000 --> 00:07:18,000
you can also directly right-click to add to the side,

118
00:07:18,000 --> 00:07:22,000
to add the side of the sleeve that has a seam relationship.

119
00:07:22,000 --> 00:07:24,000
After resetting the position,

120
00:07:24,000 --> 00:07:26,000
open the simulation,

121
00:07:28,000 --> 00:07:31,000
this dress is adjusted.

122
00:07:33,000 --> 00:07:36,000
You can select the basic line of hidden clothing,

123
00:07:36,000 --> 00:07:37,000
the internal line,

124
00:07:37,000 --> 00:07:38,000
and the hidden sticky line.

125
00:07:39,000 --> 00:07:43,000
Switch the clothing rendering type to the dense texture surface

126
00:07:43,000 --> 00:07:46,000
to check and display the clothing.

127
00:07:49,000 --> 00:07:51,000
Next, open the library,

128
00:07:51,000 --> 00:07:54,000
continue to find the selection grid file and open it.

129
00:07:59,000 --> 00:08:01,000
In order to make it easier to check,

130
00:08:01,000 --> 00:08:03,000
you can choose to hide the internal line,

131
00:08:03,000 --> 00:08:04,000
the hidden basic line,

132
00:08:04,000 --> 00:08:05,000
and the sticky line.

133
00:08:05,000 --> 00:08:08,000
The clothing rendering type can also be changed to the dense texture surface.

134
00:08:09,000 --> 00:08:12,000
You can set it according to your needs.

135
00:08:15,000 --> 00:08:18,000
When most of the fabric is in the model's body,

136
00:08:18,000 --> 00:08:21,000
or when the hitter is in the opposite direction,

137
00:08:21,000 --> 00:08:24,000
re-modeling may be very time-consuming.

138
00:08:24,000 --> 00:08:27,000
At this time, we can use the selection grid tool.

139
00:08:28,000 --> 00:08:29,000
For example,

140
00:08:29,000 --> 00:08:32,000
see the sleeves of the back shirt are worn to the arm.

141
00:08:32,000 --> 00:08:35,000
We will move the part of the plate blocked by the arm

142
00:08:35,000 --> 00:08:37,000
to the correct side.

143
00:08:37,000 --> 00:08:38,000
This can solve this problem.

144
00:08:39,000 --> 00:08:43,000
Here, we first switch the tool to the selection grid tool.

145
00:08:43,000 --> 00:08:45,000
In the 3D tool bar,

146
00:08:45,000 --> 00:08:47,000
the third tool in the first row,

147
00:08:47,000 --> 00:08:49,000
left-click and long-click.

148
00:08:49,000 --> 00:08:52,000
Here, there are three modes of selection grid tool brush,

149
00:08:52,000 --> 00:08:54,000
body, and lock.

150
00:08:54,000 --> 00:08:56,000
We use the body as an example.

151
00:08:57,000 --> 00:09:00,000
When using the selection grid tool,

152
00:09:00,000 --> 00:09:03,000
the plate will automatically display the light green grid.

153
00:09:05,000 --> 00:09:07,000
Adjust the 3D window angle

154
00:09:07,000 --> 00:09:10,000
to the area facing the mask.

155
00:09:11,000 --> 00:09:13,000
In the 3D window,

156
00:09:13,000 --> 00:09:17,000
left-click the sleeve part of the frame selection and arm mask.

157
00:09:18,000 --> 00:09:21,000
Try to select all the mask areas in the frame.

158
00:09:21,000 --> 00:09:25,000
The selected grid will now become a high-gloss light.

159
00:09:25,000 --> 00:09:27,000
Then see the 2D panel.

160
00:09:27,000 --> 00:09:30,000
The corresponding grid will also display the light green,

161
00:09:30,000 --> 00:09:32,000
indicating that it has been selected.

162
00:09:32,000 --> 00:09:33,000
It can be found that

163
00:09:33,000 --> 00:09:35,000
due to some panels being blocked by the arm,

164
00:09:35,000 --> 00:09:37,000
it cannot be selected.

165
00:09:38,000 --> 00:09:40,000
Therefore, on the 2D panel,

166
00:09:40,000 --> 00:09:42,000
in the light green center,

167
00:09:42,000 --> 00:09:45,000
there will naturally be a grid that has not been selected.

168
00:09:45,000 --> 00:09:48,000
And these grids are also where we need to select,

169
00:09:48,000 --> 00:09:51,000
and move to the outside of the arm.

170
00:09:52,000 --> 00:09:55,000
Click on the blank area to cancel the selection.

171
00:09:55,000 --> 00:09:56,000
According to the memory,

172
00:09:56,000 --> 00:09:59,000
re-select the frame selection grid on the 2D panel.

173
00:09:59,000 --> 00:10:01,000
If it is missing,

174
00:10:01,000 --> 00:10:04,000
you can press Ctrl and Shift to select more.

175
00:10:05,000 --> 00:10:06,000
If you have selected too many,

176
00:10:06,000 --> 00:10:09,000
press Ctrl to cancel the selection.

177
00:10:12,000 --> 00:10:14,000
After the selection is complete,

178
00:10:14,000 --> 00:10:17,000
in the high-gloss light in the 3D window,

179
00:10:17,000 --> 00:10:20,000
left-click to remove the positioning ball,

180
00:10:20,000 --> 00:10:23,000
and turn to the side view.

181
00:10:23,000 --> 00:10:27,000
Use the positioning ball to align the selected grid to the outside of the arm,

182
00:10:27,000 --> 00:10:29,000
wrap it around the arm,

183
00:10:29,000 --> 00:10:31,000
and then turn on the simulation.

184
00:10:31,000 --> 00:10:34,000
The sleeve mask problem on this side is fixed.

185
00:10:35,000 --> 00:10:40,000
The other side is also the same operation.

186
00:10:40,000 --> 00:10:42,000
You can practice again.

187
00:10:56,000 --> 00:10:59,000
The fold and cut of the front pants is the same.

188
00:10:59,000 --> 00:11:01,000
You can use the same technique to undo the folding in this way.

189
00:11:01,000 --> 00:11:03,000
This is the same process as before.

190
00:11:03,000 --> 00:11:06,000
Let's first determine which part of the fabric should be on top.

191
00:11:06,000 --> 00:11:10,000
Then use the selection grid tool to select this part of the grid.

192
00:11:10,000 --> 00:11:13,000
Note here

193
00:11:13,000 --> 00:11:16,000
that we need to move the original fold

194
00:11:16,000 --> 00:11:20,000
out of the upper grid.

195
00:11:20,000 --> 00:11:23,000
Combined with the green high-gloss area,

196
00:11:23,000 --> 00:11:26,000
we can determine that it should be the inside of the red line.

197
00:11:26,000 --> 00:11:28,000
The area on the left needs to be moved out.

198
00:11:28,000 --> 00:11:32,000
and pull it out.

199
00:11:32,000 --> 00:11:37,000
Note that you need to move the grid in the stop simulation state,

200
00:11:37,000 --> 00:11:45,000
otherwise it will move with the surrounding grid.

201
00:11:45,000 --> 00:11:48,000
If there is no adjustment,

202
00:11:48,000 --> 00:11:56,000
you can select the grid you need again and move it out.

203
00:11:56,000 --> 00:12:00,000
In addition, you can select the grid brush and brush tool,

204
00:12:00,000 --> 00:12:04,000
but the way of selection is different.

205
00:12:04,000 --> 00:12:08,000
The brush tool can be selected when selecting the irregular grid area,

206
00:12:08,000 --> 00:12:11,000
and it is custom-made to create a selection area.

207
00:12:11,000 --> 00:12:15,000
You can also press Ctrl and Shift to select more,

208
00:12:15,000 --> 00:12:20,000
and press Ctrl to select less.

209
00:12:20,000 --> 00:12:24,000
The brush can be applied directly on the grid,

210
00:12:24,000 --> 00:12:26,000
and you can select the grid brush

211
00:12:26,000 --> 00:12:28,000
that you want to select.

212
00:12:28,000 --> 00:12:30,000
Right-click to divide the grid,

213
00:12:30,000 --> 00:12:37,000
freeze, print, and so on.

214
00:12:37,000 --> 00:12:42,000
Finally, you can see the setting layer.

215
00:12:42,000 --> 00:12:49,000
Open this file.

216
00:12:49,000 --> 00:12:51,000
Take this layer as an example.

217
00:12:51,000 --> 00:12:54,000
Now there are two layers here.

218
00:12:54,000 --> 00:12:57,000
The belt and elastic band of this layer.

219
00:12:57,000 --> 00:13:02,000
We need to add another belt layer for this layer.

220
00:13:02,000 --> 00:13:04,000
On the belt layer,

221
00:13:04,000 --> 00:13:13,000
right-click and select the inner layer of the grid layer.

222
00:13:13,000 --> 00:13:17,000
Because the new grid layer is only attached to the original layer,

223
00:13:17,000 --> 00:13:21,000
it will exist with the elastic band of the original layer.

224
00:13:21,000 --> 00:13:23,000
Direct simulation may not be stable.

225
00:13:24,000 --> 00:13:29,000
Find the fourth tool in the second row of the 2D tool bar.

226
00:13:29,000 --> 00:13:31,000
Set the layer.

227
00:13:31,000 --> 00:13:34,000
First, click on the elastic band layer,

228
00:13:34,000 --> 00:13:38,000
then click on the inner layer of the grid layer.

229
00:13:38,000 --> 00:13:42,000
See the arrow point on the 2D layer.

230
00:13:42,000 --> 00:13:46,000
Layer 1 is the starting point of the arrow.

231
00:13:46,000 --> 00:13:48,000
The arrow points to layer 2,

232
00:13:48,000 --> 00:13:51,000
and there is a plus sign on both lines.

233
00:13:51,000 --> 00:13:52,000
This means that

234
00:13:52,000 --> 00:13:58,000
we have set the outside of the front of the plate 1 on the plate 2.

235
00:13:58,000 --> 00:14:01,000
Similarly, set the outside of the plate 2 on the plate 3.

236
00:14:01,000 --> 00:14:04,000
That is, a layer of waist fabric on the plate 1,

237
00:14:04,000 --> 00:14:06,000
a layer of elastic band on the plate 2,

238
00:14:06,000 --> 00:14:10,000
a layer of inner waist fabric on the plate 3.

239
00:14:10,000 --> 00:14:13,000
Such a structure.

240
00:14:13,000 --> 00:14:15,000
After establishing the layer relationship,

241
00:14:15,000 --> 00:14:19,000
the simulation will be very smooth.

242
00:14:19,000 --> 00:14:20,000
Here is another detail.

243
00:14:20,000 --> 00:14:22,000
We are on the left side.

244
00:14:22,000 --> 00:14:25,000
Change the clothing rendering type to the physical surface

245
00:14:25,000 --> 00:14:28,000
to distinguish the front and back of the fabric.

246
00:14:28,000 --> 00:14:30,000
You can see that

247
00:14:30,000 --> 00:14:34,000
the inner layer of the curtain is facing the outside.

248
00:14:34,000 --> 00:14:35,000
In other words,

249
00:14:35,000 --> 00:14:38,000
what we see is the opposite of the inner layer of the plate.

250
00:14:38,000 --> 00:14:43,000
If we want the inner layer to be the front of the skin,

251
00:14:43,000 --> 00:14:48,000
we need to turn the right arrow on the plate to the surface.

252
00:14:48,000 --> 00:14:49,000
After turning,

253
00:14:49,000 --> 00:14:51,000
the original layer logic changes.

254
00:14:52,000 --> 00:14:55,000
Set the plus sign on the layer line.

255
00:14:55,000 --> 00:14:59,000
It represents a plate on the outside of the front of another plate.

256
00:14:59,000 --> 00:15:01,000
Now the inner layer is turned over.

257
00:15:01,000 --> 00:15:03,000
The front and back are switched.

258
00:15:03,000 --> 00:15:06,000
The elastic band is equivalent to the back of it now.

